                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "0687a342-b45b-34e4-8ea4-f01bec3af706",
                        "entry_id": "eb4731d2-3718-3bf8-96e5-a8e6930b4c49",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Delusional."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": []
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "a7c9d786-0398-3b0b-bbd5-5694919cf929",
                        "entry_id": "eb4731d2-3718-3bf8-96e5-a8e6930b4c49",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Inappropriate to reality; forming part of a delusion."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "a47e3769-a6b4-4621-aab0-26548c3bfa7c",
                                "sense_id": "a7c9d786-0398-3b0b-bbd5-5694919cf929",
                                "text": "The poor thing was finally got off, with several delusive assurances that his absence should be short: that Mr. Edgar and Cathy would visit him, and other promises, equally ill-founded, which I invented and reiterated at intervals throughout the way."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "d00fe66c-8ae6-4949-b142-3ebfe5d81eef",
                                "sense_id": "a7c9d786-0398-3b0b-bbd5-5694919cf929",
                                "text": "[I]t seemed calculated to suggest ideas she had no intention to suggest: ideas delusive and disturbing."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "aa4839e4-abb2-4b41-886a-58b0d2e35ef7",
                                "sense_id": "a7c9d786-0398-3b0b-bbd5-5694919cf929",
                                "text": "I opened my eyes, I rubbed them, and found I was not asleep but thoroughly awake. Nevertheless, I felt my head and breast to satisfy myself whether it was I myself who was there or some empty delusive phantom; but touch, feeling, the collected thoughts that passed through my mind, all convinced me that I was the same then and there that I am this moment."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
